    "summary": "Families displaced by fighting in Hiran region are struggling with food shortages and homelessness after fleeing multiple locations. Many have arrived in Coomaad with few belongings and no means of support.",
    "content": "Families displaced by ongoing clashes between Al-Shabaab and Somali government forces in Hiran region are experiencing severe food shortages and homelessness, according to local reports. Many have fled multiple times in search of safety and are now arriving in Coomaad, near Mataban, with few possessions and limited ability to support themselves.\n\nOne such case is Nuriya Mohamed Bare, a 51-year-old mother of eight, who reached Coomaad on 10 October after walking from Hees. Her family had been displaced repeatedly by conflict, and Hees was seized by Al-Shabaab and later recaptured by the Somali National Army. The repeated displacement has left families like hers in a state of constant uncertainty.\n\nThe fighting in Hiran region is part of a broader conflict between Somali government forces, supported by local militias and international partners, and Al-Shabaab militants. The region has seen periodic offensives and counter-offensives, leading to civilian displacement. Aid agencies have warned that access to those in need is often hampered by insecurity.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the plight of displaced families in Hiran is a growing concern. Many diaspora members have relatives in the region and contribute remittances that are vital for survival. The latest displacement adds to the already large number of internally displaced persons in Somalia, straining resources and highlighting the need for sustained humanitarian support.\n\nDiaspora organizations and international partners are calling for increased assistance to reach those affected. However, ongoing conflict and limited access make it difficult to deliver aid. The situation remains fluid, with families like Nuriya's facing an uncertain future.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Ergo here: https://radioergo.org/en/2026/11/havoc-for-civilians-caught-in-the-crossfire-of-conflict-in-hiran-region/",
